{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":305154,"duration_api_ms":302478,"num_turns":28,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cecd22a8-cc15-4952-9a3f-c69e80f16231","total_cost_usd":1.3443253499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":729,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59888,"cache_read_input_tokens":1067395,"output_tokens":7094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":729,"outputTokens":7094,"cacheReadInputTokens":1067395,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59888,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0889925000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2666,"outputTokens":8391,"cacheReadInputTokens":1431981,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54011,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25533284999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all changes across 14 files covering: (1) new reproduction suppression parameters (TAN/NO2 full-suppression, low-temp ramp width, shared mineral floor/divisor for gh_mineral_factor), (2) substrate oxygenation refactor (habitat registry threading, root respiration demand baseline), (3) invariant validation additions, (4) preset/TOML/scenario plumbing, (5) comprehensive test additions. One confirmed test failure exists, traceable to a behavioral regression in TAN/NO2 suppression steepness. One duplicate parameter entry exists in preset validation. Overall the implementation is well-structured with good test coverage for the new parameters.","amendments":[{"body":"The default values for `tan_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` (2.0) and `no2_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` (1.0) produce effective suppression spans of 1.0 and 0.5 respectively, whereas the old formulas used `threshold * 2.0` giving spans of 2.0 and 1.0. This makes TAN/NO2 reproduction suppression 2x more aggressive than the prior behavior. This causes `controlled_ideal_reproduction_path_still_hatches` to fail (readiness 0.339, expected [0.35, 0.85]). Either adjust the defaults to preserve the old curve shape (TAN full-suppression = 3.0, NO2 full-suppression = 1.5), or update the test envelope bounds to accommodate the intentionally steeper suppression. The choice should be explicit and documented.","rationale":"This is a confirmed test failure caused by a behavioral regression. The old formula `(1.0 - excess / (threshold * 2.0))` had a span equal to `threshold * 2.0`. The new formula `(1.0 - excess / (full_suppression - threshold))` uses a span of `full_suppression - threshold`. With default TAN values (threshold=1.0, full=2.0), old span=2.0 vs new span=1.0. This doubles the suppression slope for any given TAN excess above threshold, and analogously for NO2."},{"body":"`low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c` appears in both the non-negative validation list (line ~770) and the strictly-positive validation list (line ~930) in `ShrimpPreset::validate()`. The non-negative check is redundant since the positive check is stricter. Remove the entry from the first (non-negative) list to avoid confusion about which constraint actually governs.","rationale":"The duplicate entry suggests a copy-paste error during parameter addition. While not a correctness bug (both checks pass for any valid value), it creates maintenance confusion about which validation tier the parameter belongs to, and the non-negative check can never fire independently since the strictly-positive check is evaluated for the same value."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ba7d08b4-0557-4c81-8859-0591f74b7ce6"}
